"I can’t provide a hidden chain-of-thought or internal scratchpad. Instead, here is a concise summary of the extraction approach used: I parsed the source text into explicit product capabilities, constraints, integrations, and quality attributes; grouped them into Functional Requirements (user-visible behaviors, workflows, data retrieval, personalization, notifications, sharing, authentication, module behavior, rights-aware stream display) and Non-Functional Requirements (platform scope, startup performance, real-time behavior where framed as quality, reliability under poor networks, offline usability, scalability to 100,000 concurrent users, UI accessibility/directness as usability, consistency despite server updates, testing/support process, continuous improvement from feedback, GDPR compliance). I then removed duplicates where the same idea appeared twice (e.g., live results/live ticker in real time) and kept distinct aspects separate when they were independently testable (e.g., selecting favorite teams vs selecting preferred sports channels; notifications activation vs favorite-team-triggered notifications; live stream links vs geo/rights gating). IDs were assigned sequentially without gaps."